    "body": "### Problem\n\nIf in Normal mode the recently used Visual mode was linewise, `vin` or `van` starts in Visual Line too, instead of starting the `v` mode as typed. \n\nWhile not fixed a workaround (custom keymap) can contain calling `vim.cmd.normal('v')` afterwards (if `api.nvim_get_mode().mode ~= 'v'`). \n\ncc @altermo \n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nFor example in the Nvim project\n\n- `nvim --clean runtime/ftplugin/ch.lua`\n- type `V<Esc>vin`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nAssuming that the first line is `vim.bo.commentstring = '// %s'`, only `vim` is selected. \n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nv0.13.0-dev-1140+gfbcb7a056c\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nn/a\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nDebian Sid\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nalacritty\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nalacritty\n\n### Installation\n\nfrom repo",
